{%- comment -%}
  Product card: a tile with the image and a tag (snippets/mu-badges: coming soon / sold out / pre-order, see mu-pp-pre / sale, or % off with Cards > Sale badge, see mu-sale-pct / new; New and Sale take Cards > Badge colours when set, the rest use the scheme; coming soon reads custom.release_date; Cards > Badge position moves the badges to a row above the title instead).
  Below it the title (Cards > Title size), the star rating (Cards > Show rating; Show empty ratings gives unrated products empty stars and "No reviews", see mu-rating), the price, up to 4 colour dots (from option swatches; each dot links to its colour: in a combined listing that colour's product, otherwise this product with the first available variant of that colour)
  and, with Cards > Show quick view button, an outline button that opens quick view (sections/mu-quick-add, assets/mu-quick-add.js), or adds a product without options straight to the bag (quick buy, below).
  With Theme settings > Cards: the second media fades in on hover (mouse only; a Shopify-hosted video plays muted,
  an external video shows its preview image; off = the hover motion applies to the first image), and product tags that start with the
  badge prefix (default "badge:", e.g. "badge:Staff pick") show as extra badges, skipping one that repeats the tag (e.g. "badge:Pre-order" on a pre-order).
  Coming-soon products and products that can only be bought with a purchase option (selling plan) keep the button, but it links to the product page.
  Card style (Theme settings > Cards): level fills the card with its level's gradient, the image stands on it and price
  and button sit on a calm chip; plain keeps the image on a soft band. Products with no level use the scheme. In
  Product colors only mode the accent colour (mu-tone) stands in for the level, and the label strip shows custom.short_name.
  Label stands the product's cut-out (custom.cutout, else the featured image) on a flat square panel over a printed
  strip with its level; with the hover image on, the featured photo fills the panel on hover.
  Pass product. Optional: sizes (the image sizes attribute; 'rail' for the 4-up rails of Featured collection and the
  product-page rails, measured from their layout), eager (true for cards above the fold), fp ('high' for the first row's images), heading ('h2' where
  the card sits straight under the page h1, as in the collection and search grids; default 'h3').
  layout 'lineup' renders snippets/mu-card-lineup instead (numbered row). Pass lineup_index, lineup_numbers
  (outline or solid) and show_sub (first selling plan price).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if layout == 'lineup' -%}
  {%- render 'mu-card-lineup', product: product, index: lineup_index, numbers: lineup_numbers, show_sub: show_sub, eager: eager -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img = product.featured_media.preview_image
  assign title_tag = heading | default: 'h3'
  assign img_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 990px) 25vw, 45vw'
  if sizes == 'rail'
    assign c_mob = 'calc(66vw - 34px)'
    if settings.card_mobile_size == 'compact'
      assign c_mob = 'calc(47vw - 24px)'
    endif
    capture img_sizes
      render 'mu-sizes', sub: 64, f: 0.25, tab: '28vw', mob: c_mob
    endcapture
  endif
  assign load = 'lazy'
  if eager
    assign load = 'eager'
  endif
  assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign coming = false
  assign release = product.metafields.custom.release_date.value
  if release != blank
    assign release_s = release | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    if release_s > now_s
      assign coming = true
    endif
  endif
  assign img2 = blank
  assign vid2 = blank
  assign fill2 = false
  if settings.card_style == 'label'
    assign cut = product.metafields.custom.cutout.value
    if cut != blank
      assign img = cut.preview_image | default: cut
      if settings.card_hover_image and product.featured_media.preview_image
        assign img2 = product.featured_media.preview_image
        assign fill2 = true
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if settings.card_hover_image and img and fill2 == false
    for m in product.media offset: 1
      if m.preview_image
        assign img2 = m.preview_image
        if m.media_type == 'video'
          assign vid2 = m
        endif
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if vid2 != blank
    assign vsrc = blank
    assign vh = 0
    for src in vid2.sources
      if src.format == 'mp4' and src.height <= 720 and src.height > vh
        assign vsrc = src
        assign vh = src.height
      endif
    endfor
    if vsrc == blank
      assign vsrc = vid2.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4' | first
    endif
    if vsrc == blank
      assign vid2 = blank
    endif
  endif
  assign dots = blank
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign has_swatch = false
    for value in option.values
      if value.swatch.color or value.swatch.image
        assign has_swatch = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if has_swatch
      assign dots = option
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- liquid
  assign badge_pos = settings.card_badge_position | default: 'image'
  assign title_size = settings.card_title_size | default: 'medium'
  capture hs
    render 'mu-level', product: product
  endcapture
  assign lv = hs | split: '|' | first | plus: 0
  assign hsc = hs | split: '|' | last | plus: 0
  assign style = settings.card_style | default: 'plain'
  assign card_cls = 'mu-card mu-card--' | append: style
  assign tone_sty = ''
  if settings.scale_mode == 'colors'
    capture tn
      render 'mu-tone', product: product
    endcapture
    assign tn = tn | split: '|'
    if tn[0] != blank
      assign card_cls = card_cls | append: ' ' | append: tn[0]
      assign tone_sty = tn[1]
    else
      assign card_cls = card_cls | append: ' mu-card--unrated'
    endif
  elsif lv > 0
    assign card_cls = card_cls | append: ' mu-h-' | append: lv
    if hsc == 2
      assign card_cls = card_cls | append: ' mu-s2'
    endif
  else
    assign card_cls = card_cls | append: ' mu-card--unrated'
  endif
-%}
{%- capture tags_html -%}{%- render 'mu-badges', product: product, coming: coming -%}{%- endcapture -%}
<article class="{{ card_cls }}{% if settings.card_quick_view %} mu-card--qv{% endif %} mu-card--t-{{ title_size }} mu-card--b-{{ badge_pos }}" style="--l: {{ lv }};{% if tone_sty != blank %} {{ tone_sty }}{% endif %}">
  <div class="mu-card__media">
    <a class="mu-card__img-link" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- if img -%}
        {%- assign ar_style = '--ar: ' | append: img.aspect_ratio | append: ';' -%}
        {% render 'mu-img', image: img, max: 1200, sizes: img_sizes, loading: load, fp: fp, class: 'mu-card__img', style: ar_style %}
        {%- if vid2 != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%} Shopify-hosted video as the second media: nothing loads until a mouse hovers the card (mu-card-video.js), then it plays muted, inline and looped and fades in once playing. {%- endcomment -%}
          <video class="mu-card__img mu-card__img--alt mu-card__vid" data-src="{{ vsrc.url }}" muted playsinline loop preload="none" disablepictureinpicture aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></video>
          <script src="{{ 'mu-card-video.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
        {%- elsif fill2 -%}
          {% render 'mu-img', image: img2, max: 1200, sizes: img_sizes, class: 'mu-card__img mu-card__img--alt mu-card__img--fill' %}
        {%- elsif img2 != blank -%}
          {%- assign ar_style2 = '--ar: ' | append: img2.aspect_ratio | append: ';' -%}
          {% render 'mu-img', image: img2, max: 1200, sizes: img_sizes, class: 'mu-card__img mu-card__img--alt', style: ar_style2 %}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'mu-placeholder' }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
    {%- render 'mu-stickers', product: product -%}
    {%- if badge_pos == 'image' -%}{{ tags_html }}{%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- if style == 'label' and lv > 0 -%}
    <div class="mu-card__label">{%- render 'mu-rung', product: product, size: 'sm' -%}</div>
  {%- elsif style == 'label' and tone_sty != blank and product.metafields.custom.short_name != blank -%}
    <div class="mu-card__label"><span class="mu-card__accent">{{ product.metafields.custom.short_name.value | escape }}</span></div>
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="mu-card__body">
    {%- if badge_pos == 'title' -%}{{ tags_html }}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.scale_on_cards and style != 'label' -%}{%- render 'mu-rung', product: product, size: 'sm' -%}{%- endif -%}
    <{{ title_tag }} class="mu-card__title mu-scale-type"><a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a></{{ title_tag }}>
    {%- render 'mu-rating', product: product, show: settings.card_rating, empty: settings.card_rating_empty, class: 'mu-card__rating' -%}
    {%- if dots != blank -%}
      {%- assign dot_index = dots.position | minus: 1 -%}
      <ul class="mu-card__dots" role="list" aria-label="{{ dots.name | escape }}">
        {%- for value in dots.values limit: 4 -%}
          {%- comment -%} Every dot links to its colour. Combined listings: a colour that is its own product (option_value.product_url) links to it. Otherwise the dot links to this product with the first available variant of that colour selected (first variant if none is available). The colour shown on the card gets aria-current. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign dot_url = ''
            assign sib_url = value.product_url | append: ''
            if sib_url != '' and sib_url != product.url
              assign dot_url = sib_url
            endif
            if dot_url == ''
              assign dot_variant = nil
              for dv in product.variants
                if dv.options[dot_index] == value.name
                  if dv.available
                    assign dot_variant = dv
                    break
                  elsif dot_variant == nil
                    assign dot_variant = dv
                  endif
                endif
              endfor
              if dot_variant
                assign dot_url = dot_variant.url
              else
                assign dot_url = product.url
              endif
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="mu-card__dot mu-card__dot--link" title="{{ value | escape }}" style="
            {%- if value.swatch.image -%}background-image: url({{ value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 48 }});{%- else -%}background-color: {{ value.swatch.color }};{%- endif -%}
          ">
            <a href="{{ dot_url }}"{% if value.selected %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}><span class="visually-hidden">{{ value | escape }}</span></a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if dots.values.size > 4 -%}<li class="mu-card__more">+{{ dots.values.size | minus: 4 }}</li>{%- endif -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="mu-card__chip">
      <div class="mu-card__money">
        <p class="mu-card__price">{% render 'mu-price', product: product %}</p>
        {%- if v.unit_price_measurement -%}
          <p class="mu-card__unit">{% render 'mu-unit-price', price: v.unit_price, measurement: v.unit_price_measurement %}</p>
        {%- elsif v.title != 'Default Title' and product.variants.size > 1 -%}
          <p class="mu-card__unit">{{ v.title | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if settings.card_quick_view -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign qv_label = settings.card_quick_view_label | strip
          if qv_label == blank
            assign qv_label = 'products.quick_view_button' | t
          endif
        -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Quick buy (Cards > Add single-variant products directly): a product with only one variant (no options, or options
          with one value each, like Size: 200 g) that can be bought outright adds straight to the bag (assets/mu-quick-add.js). Anything risky keeps quick view: gift cards
          (recipient form), purchase options, and out-of-stock selling (pre-orders). Adds the B2B minimum when there is one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign qb = false
          if settings.card_quick_buy and product.variants.size == 1 and v.available and product.gift_card? == false and product.selling_plan_groups.size == 0
            assign qb = true
            if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy == 'continue' and v.inventory_quantity <= 0
              assign qb = false
            endif
          endif
          assign qb_label = settings.card_quick_buy_label | strip
          if qb_label == blank
            assign qb_label = 'products.add_short' | t
          endif
        -%}
          {%- if coming or product.requires_selling_plan -%}
            <a class="mu-btn mu-btn--sm mu-card__qv" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ qv_label | escape }}<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ product.title | escape }}</span></a>
          {%- elsif qb -%}
            <button class="mu-btn mu-btn--sm mu-card__qv" type="button" data-quick-add="{{ product.url }}" data-quick-buy="{{ v.id }}" data-qty="{{ v.quantity_rule.min | default: 1 }}">{{ qb_label | escape }}<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ product.title | escape }}. {{ 'products.quick_buy_hint' | t }}</span></button>
            <p class="mu-card__msg" role="status" data-qb-msg></p>
          {%- else -%}
            <button class="mu-btn mu-btn--sm mu-card__qv" type="button" data-quick-add="{{ product.url }}" aria-haspopup="dialog">{{ qv_label | escape }}<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ product.title | escape }}</span></button>
          {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
{%- endif -%}
